\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, speak to me, that I may speak
\par In living echoes of Thy tone;
\par As Thou hast sought, so let me seek
\par Thy erring children lost and lone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O lead me, Lord, that I may lead
\par The wandering and the wavering feet;
\par O feed me, Lord, that I may feed
\par Thy hungering ones with manner sweet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O strengthen me, that, while I stand
\par Firm on the rock, and strong in Thee,
\par I may stretch out a loving hand
\par To wrestlers with the troubled sea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O teach me, Lord, that I may teach
\par The precious things Thou dost impart;
\par And wing my words, that may reach
\par The hidden depths of many a heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O give Thine own sweet rest to me,
\par That I may speak with soothing power
\par A word in season, as from Thee,
\par To weary ones in needful hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O fill me with Thy fullness, Lord,
\par Until my very eye o'erflow
\par In kindling thought and glowing word,
\par Thy love to tell, Thy praise to show.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O use me, Lord, use even me,
\par Just as Thou wilt, and when, and where,
\par Until Thy blessed face I see,
\par Thy rest,Thy joy,Thy glory share. Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

